# --- decaying categories, pinned correct memory -------------------------------
# `pinned: true` on the OLD correct memory. A pinned row's decay factor is
# exactly 1.0 at any age, so these are the fixture's answer to "an old-but-correct
# memory in a decaying category must still win": it wins because the user pinned
# it, which is the one control production offers against a category that decays.
# Named in recencytrap_test.go's trapMustWinScenarios; renaming one without
# updating that list fails the test, and an empty list fails it too.
{"name":"vault_one_way","category":"decision","pinned":true,"correct":{"content":"We decided the vault mirror is one-way: nothing is ever written back out of it.","age_days":600},"traps":[{"content":"Filed an issue asking for a reverse sync that would import edits out of the vault.","age_days":5}],"probes":[{"text":"does anything get written back out of the vault"}]}
